1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Capt. Lucas GARCIA [74],[739],[1788],[1867] 
2 CONT *was born about 1576. 
2 CONT *Lucas Garcia was one of the 15 settlers who came with Diego Montemayor when he founded the city of Monterrey in 1596. 
2 CONT *Parents: Baltasar de SOSA and Ines RODRIGUEZ.
2 CONT *Spouse: Juliana de QUINTANILLA. Juliana de QUINTANILLA and Capt. Lucas GARCIA [365] were married about 1596. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children were: 
2 CONT *1. Diego GARCIA de Quintanilla, 
2 CONT *2. Juana GARCIA (aka Juana de Farias), 
2 CONT *3. Bernardo Garcia de SOSA, 
2 CONT *4. Ana de QUINTANILLA, 
2 CONT *5. Capt. Tomas GARCIA de QUINTANILLA, 
2 CONT *6. Lucas GARCIA, 
2 CONT *7. Nicolas GARCIA, 
2 CONT *8. Bartolome GARCIA.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b88.html#P947
2 CONT
2 CONT ==========================================
2 CONT
2 CONT [5]	Mariana SOSA SALDIVAR m. Diego GARCIA DE-QUINTANILLA, (son of Lucas GARCIA RODRIGUEZ and Juliana QUINTANILLA FARIAS).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.vsalgs.org/stnemgenealogy/alonsoes.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT From the work of Miguel A. Ayala (webcached 01/02/2013):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/a/y/a/Miguel-A-Ayala-TX/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0192.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Lucas Garcia (b. Abt. 1576)
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Lucas Garcia (son of Baltazar Castano de Sosa and Inés Rodriguez de Montemayor) was born Abt. 1576 in Nueva Galicia, Tampico, Mexico. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Juliana de Quintanilla on Abt. 1596, daughter of Juan de Farias, (El Portugese), Capt. and Maria Ana de Trevino.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucas García, Portuguese, complete [sic] brother of Diego Rodríguez, sons of Baltasar de Sosa and Inés Rodríguez, inhabitants of Saltillo; husband of Juliana de Quintanilla, who was an entire [sic] sister of José de Treviño and of
2 CONC  Sebastiana de Treviño, this last one wife of the major justice Diego Rodríguez, her uncle. He was one of the founders of the city of Monterrey. “Lucas García was a translator of the Huachichila language. In 1606, he accompanied D
2 CONC on Francisco de Urdiñola in the punishment of the Indians who sacrificed Fray Martín de Altamira in the river of Nadadores in Coahuila. He had the rank of captain and he had diverse charges in Monterrey: town councillor (1599, 160
2 CONC 1, 1606 & 1630); mayor first class (1607, 1627 & 1628) and mayor second class (1602, 1611 & 1624). He was, furthermore, procurer in 1616.”243
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.library.ci.corpus-christi.tx.us/newkingdom/reinochapter4p70.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Capt. Lucas Garcia:
2 CONT
2 CONT Date born 2: Abt. 1576
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Capt. Lucas Garcia and Juliana de Quintanilla:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Abt. 1596
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Capt. Lucas Garcia and Juliana de Quintanilla are:
2 CONT *1. Ana Garcia de Quintanilla, b. Abt. 1625, d. July 08, 1684.
2 CONT *2. +Diego Garcia de Quintanilla, b. 1600, Monterrey, Nuevo León, México, d. 1669.
2 CONT *3. Tomás García Quintañilla, b. 1609.
2 CONT *4. Lucas García Quintañilla, b. 1611.
2 CONT *5. Nicolás García Quintañilla, b. 1613.
2 CONT *6. Bartolome García Quintañilla, b. 1615.
2 CONT *7. +Juana de Farias Garcia, b. date unknown.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
