1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Villanueva de Cavazos, Lilia E.'''''Testamentos Coloniales de Monterrey''''', Monterrey, Nuevo León, Mexico, 1991, pages 18-22. [Ramo Civil, Vol. 5, Exp. 22, Folio 3]   ...  The '''1643 will of Capitán Miguel De Mo
2 CONC ntemayor'''  (dated 11 October 1643) cites his parents, his wife Mónica Rodríguez, her parents Capitán Diego Rodríguez and Sebastiana de Tremiño, a deceased son Lucas, as well as his legitimate children '''Diego''', Margarita, Pet
2 CONC rona, María, Francisco, Domingo, José, Bernardo, and Mateo.  Additionally, the will cites two "bastard" daughters: María, wife of Juan Maldonado, and Juana, wife of Andrés de Charles.  Further, the will directs that he be interred
2 CONC  in Monterrey's Iglesia Parroquial and states that he is ill near to death.
