2 CONT Leonardo LONGORIA died on 20 May 1837.2363,2364 He may be the Leonardo Longoria de la Garza who received the "El Rincon del Grullo" land grant consisting of 28,642 acres in present day Kleberg County, Texas. The land grant was mad
2 CONC e by the State of Tamaulipas on April 11, 1848. The Bourland and Miller Report notes that "Juliana Lopez de Longoria applies for herself and the other heirs of her deceased husband Leonardo Longoria de la Garza for 6 leagues of la
2 CONC nd originally granted by the State of Tamaulipas to the said Garza, decd.; said tract of land is called "El Rincon del Grullo". Parents: Jose Miguel LONGORIA Hinojosa and Encarnacion de la GARZA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Feliciana Juliana LOPEZ. Feliciana Juliana LOPEZ and Leonardo LONGORIA were married on 18 May 1812 in Matamoros, Tamaulipas, Mexico.133,2365 Children were: Maria Vicenta LONGORIA Lopez, Maria Catarina LONGORIA Lopez, Perfe
2 CONC cta LONGORIA Lopez, Maria Melchora LONGORIA Lopez, Agapito LONGORIA Lopez, Maria Candida LONGORIA, Jose Encarnacion LONGORIA Lopez, Jose Santiago LONGORIA Lopez, Maria Guadalupe LONGORIA Lopez, Maria Francisca LONGORIA Lopez, Mari
2 CONC a Guadalupe LONGORIA Lopez, Esteban LONGORIA Lopez, Jacobo LONGORIA Lopez.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Marcela SALINAS Lopez. Marcela SALINAS Lopez and Leonardo LONGORIA were married on 12 May 1827 in Matamoros, Tamaulipas, Mexico.499,2366,2367 Ancestry.com shows a marriage date of May 2, 1827 for Leonardo Longoria and Marc
2 CONC ela Salinas; the Indice de Casamientos from the Frank Cushman Pierce Collection shows the marriage date as May 12, 1827. However, there is reason to believe both sources are in error. Leonardo Longoria and Juliana Lopez had at lea
2 CONC st 6 children after April 1827, and Juliana Lopez in the 1850's referred to herself as the widow of Leonardo Longoria de la Garza. The Church would not have sanctioned a second marriage if the first wife were still alive.
2 CONT
