1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.currays.net/Gonzalez%20Web%20Project/ps03/ps03_461.htm  ...  Martha Duron Jimenez and Ignacio Narro Etchegaray. ''DICCIONARIO BIOGRAFICO DE SALTILLO'', Mayo 1995, page 128:   '''Juan NAVARRO, a founder o
2 CONC f Saltillo, native of Navarra, was known by the nickname El Vizcaino [a reference to his Basque origins]'''. He '''married Dona Maria RODRIGUEZ, daughter of Capitan Baltasar de SOSA and Dona Ines RODRIGUEZ'''. Their '''children we
2 CONC re:''' '''Beatriz''', whose first marriage was to Capitan Alonso ALBORNOZ and second marriage was to Capitan Bernabe de las CASAS; '''Ursula''', who married Capitan Diego SANCHEZ; '''Melchora''', who married Capitan Martin SANCHEZ
2 CONC ; '''Ines''', who married Capitan Francisco MARTINEZ GUAJARDO; '''Maria''', who married Capitan Jose de TREVINO; '''Francisca''', who married Capitan Juan TARANCO VALLEJO; '''Martin''', who married Maria ROJO de las RUELAS; and ''
2 CONC 'Mariana''' NAVARRO RODRIGUEZ, who married Capitan Marcos GONZALEZ HIDALGO.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''_________________________________'''
2 CONT
2 CONT in 1561 was owner of "estancia" in the valle of Sichu.  Was given land in 1578 in Parras, Coah. On Sept 2 1591 was made Alcalde of Santiago de Saltillo
2 CONT
