1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Beatriz Navarro''' was born about 1564
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT #Alonso de Sosa Albornoz, about 1585
2 CONT #Bernabe de las Casas, about 1602
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatriz and Alonso had one child: 
2 CONT #Ana de Sosa Albornoz
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatriz and Bernabe de las Casas had five children:
2 CONT #Beatriz de las Casas
2 CONT #Juliana de las Casas
2 CONT #Maria de las Casas
2 CONT #Alferez Mayor Marcos de las Casas
2 CONT #Bernabe de las Casas
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatriz was the daughter of Juan Navarro and Maria Rodreguez.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatriz was a member of the Juan de Oñate Expedition.  Beatriz and Bernabe de las Casas met in New Mexico, during its conquest by Juan de Oñate, and she married him after her first husband was murdered by a member of the 1598 New 
2 CONC Mexico Expedition.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Links ==
2 CONT
