2 CONT '''______________________'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedro the younger was born in Nuevo Leon between 1612 and 161i5. Between 1642 and 1676 served as alderman, procurer, and assistant mayor (1659 and 1683) of Monterrey. His hacienda was Hacienda de San Nicolas, now called San Nicola
2 CONC s de los Garzas. Awarded an encomienda in 1663. It is said of him "Pedro de la Garza, resident of this kingdom, who is a meritorious person and the son of a conquistador; and who has served His Majesty with full approbation, in al
2 CONC l the occasions that have offered themselves to be in the royal service as a good soldier and as his loyal vassal." In 1691, the governor of Nuevo Leon made reference to him "as a meritorious peron, old, and citizen of the said ki
2 CONC ngdom, and that since his first years, he has served His Majesty in it with very well known merits, risking his person on different occasions against the Indians rebelling against the crown." (Mendirichaga 1989,14)  My direct ance
2 CONC stor, Ines de la Garza, his daughter, would marry Jose Martinez, the founder of San Antonio de los Martinez, later the villa of Marin. Ref: "Conquistadores and Crypto-Jews of Monterrey" David T. Raphael (c. 2001)
2 CONT --------------------
