2 CONT
2 CONT Act of Foundation of Monterrey 1638, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico 
2 CONT
2 CONT The charter of the Metropolitan City of Our Lady of Monterrey, is dated September 20, 1596, issued by the Captain Diego de Montemayor (founder of it), and signed by the clerk Diego Díaz de Berlanga.This important document that sup
2 CONC ports its validity in the Ordinances for the founding of towns, villages and cities in the territory of Spanish rule, tells the location of these royal lands, and establishes the creation of a council to govern the new city. The t
2 CONC ranscript is from the Book Volume 1 Proceedings of City Council, as the original document is not within the Acquis. It presents the image of the document that contains a copy of the letter made original founding in 1638 by the not
2 CONC ary Juan de Abrego. In the name of God Almighty and the glorious and blessed Mary ever Virgin, Mother of God and Our Lady. This public instrument know how many founding charter [Vieren] how I, Diego de Montemayor treasurer of the 
2 CONC Exchequer of the New Kingdom of León, lieutenant governor and captain-general for the rebuilding of it by the king our lord, mindful of the causes and the reasons people gave for coming to this valley of Extremadura and kingdom fo
2 CONC r its population and pacification of the natives of him, try spreading the holy gospel and the kingdoms and dominions of His Majesty and his royal heritage is increased, which cause and zeal is mine and I moved to this effect and 
