1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 70. CAPTAIN AMBROCIO4 DE CEPEDA-DE-LA-CASAS-DE-LA-FUENTE (JUANA3 DE-LA-FUENTE-MARTINEZ, FRANCISCA2 MARTINEZ-GUAJARDO-NAVARRO-RODRIGUEZ, JUAN-FRANCISCO1 MARTINEZ-GUAJARDO) was born in Saltillo, Coahuila, Mexico, and
2 CONC  died Aft. June 06, 1673 in Saltillo, Coahuila, Mexico. He met (1) JUANA-MICAELA SAENZ-DEL-VALLE, daughter of DIEGO SAENZ-TREVINO and CLARA DEL VALLE. He married (2) ANA DE SALDIVAR-SOSA Abt. 1672 in Saltillo, Coahulia, Mexico, da
2 CONC ughter of VICENTE DE SALDIVAR-Y-REZA and MARIA DE SOSA. She was born in Saltillo, Coahuila, Mexico, and died in Saltillo, Coahuila, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for CAPTAIN AMBROCIO DE CEPEDA-DE-LA-CASAS-DE-LA-FUENTE:
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:Mil Familias III by Rodolfo Gonzalez de la Garza. Page 23.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for ANA DE SALDIVAR-SOSA:
2 CONT
2 CONT In the book, Mil Familias III, by Rodolfo Gonzalez de la Garza, she is listed as a descendent of the Don Alonso of Estrada, The Duke of Aragon. Page 99. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, she is a descendent of the Onate-Zaldivar Family of Zacatecas and New Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes for AMBROCIO DE CEPEDA-DE-LA-CASAS-DE-LA-FUENTE and ANA DE SALDIVAR-SOSA:
2 CONT
2 CONT Origen de los Fundadores de Texas, Nuevo Mexico, Coahulia, y Nuevo Leon, by Guillermo Garmendia Leal. (page 125).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mil Familias III by Rodolfo Gonzalez de la Garza. Page 326.
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriage investigations of the Diocese of Guadalajara, Provinces of Coahulia, Nuevo Leon, Nuevo Santander, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT With All Arms, A Study of a Kindred Group, by Carl Laurence Duaine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of AMBROCIO DE CEPEDA-DE-LA-CASAS-DE-LA-FUENTE and JUANA-MICAELA SAENZ-DEL-VALLE are:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. AMBROCIO5 DE CEPEDA-SAENZ, m. MARIA SAN-MIGUEL-ADAME.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. CLARA-JOSEFA SAENZ, m. FRANCISCO TREVINO-CHAPA, April 25, 1701, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico; b. November 24, 1681, Sagrario Metropolitano, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for CLARA-JOSEFA SAENZ:
2 CONT
2 CONT A.K.A. Clara Josefa de Cepeda.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes for CLARA-JOSEFA SAENZ and FRANCISCO TREVINO-CHAPA:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage source from the book, Index to the Marriage Investigations of the Diocese of Guadalajara,
2 CONT
2 CONT by Raul J, Guerra, Jr., Nadine M. Vasquez, Baldomero Vela, Jr. Page 272.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. JUANA CEPEDA-SAENZ, b. Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico; m. ANTONIO GARCIA-DE-SEPULVEDA, June 26, 1693, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico; b. 1673, Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes for JUANA CEPEDA-SAENZ and ANTONIO GARCIA-DE-SEPULVEDA:
2 CONT
2 CONT Index to the Marriage Investigations of the Diocese of Guadalajara by Raul J. Guerra, Jr., Nadine M. Vasquez, Baldomero Vela, Jr. Page 36.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of AMBROCIO DE CEPEDA-DE-LA-CASAS-DE-LA-FUENTE and ANA DE SALDIVAR-SOSA are:
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. DIEGO5 DE CEPEDA-SALDIVAR.
2 CONT
2 CONT 223. v. JULIANA DE CEPEDA-SALDIVAR.
2 CONT
2 CONT vi. JUSEPE DE CEPEDA-SALDIVAR.
2 CONT
2 CONT vii. MARGARITA DE CEPEDA-SALDIVAR.
2 CONT
2 CONT viii. SANTIAGO DE CEPEDA-SALDIVAR.
2 CONT
2 CONT ix. ALONSO DE CEPEDA-SALDIVAR.
2 CONT
2 CONT x. ANA DE CEPEDA-SALDIVAR, b. Abt. 1655, Saltillo, Coahuila, Mexico; d. Aft. October 11, 1691, Saltillo, Coahuila, Mexico; m. PEDRO DE ESPINO-DEL-SIXTO, Abt. 1686, Saltillo, Coahulia, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for ANA DE CEPEDA-SALDIVAR:
2 CONT
2 CONT On October 11, 1691 she signed her last will and testament. Source: Mil Familias III by Rodolfo Gonzalez de la Garza. Page 24.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is a descendent of the Onate-Zaldivar Family of Zacatecas and New Mexico.
2 CONT
