2 CONT v. CAPTAIN LUIS ANTONIO MENCHACA-URRUTIA, b. 1713, San Juan Bautista del Rio Grande , el Presido del Norte, Coahulia,Mexico; d. 29 Sep 1793, San Francisco Ranch, Karnes/Wilson County, Texas; m. MARIA-IGNACIA-AGUSTINA NUNEZ-FLORES,
2 CONC  27 Feb 1744/45, San Fernando, San Antonio, Bexar County, Texas; b. 1731, San Fernando, San Antonio, Bexar County, Texas; d. Aft. 12 Sep 1800, San Francisco Ranch, Karnes/Wilson County, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for CAPTAIN LUIS ANTONIO MENCHACA-URRUTIA:
2 CONT
2 CONT Appointed Captain of the Presidio at Bexar in 1763. A prominent ranch owner. The 1779 census for the province of Texas revealed him to be the wealthiest and top cattle owner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:San Antonio de Bexar by Jesus F. De La Teja
2 CONT
2 CONT (Estado General de la Provincia de Texas)
2 CONT
2 CONT Served as justicia mayor of the Villa of San Fernando.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:The Makers of San Antonio, By Frederich C. Chabot.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for MARIA-IGNACIA-AGUSTINA NUNEZ-FLORES:
2 CONT
2 CONT Will signed on September 12, 1800. Power of Attorney was given to her son, Luis Mariano Menchaca and brother, Felix Menchaca. Ignacio Maria Luzaro signed for her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:Will and Inventories of Bexar County, Texas - San Antonio Genealogical and Historical Society.
2 CONT
2 CONT San Antonio de Bexar, by Jesus F. de la Teja.
2 CONT
2 CONT Endnotes
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Brøderbund Software, Inc., World Family Tree Vol. 6, Ed. 1, (Release date: August 22, 1996), "CD-ROM," Tree #4100, Date of Import: Sep 10, 1998.
2 CONT
2 CONT Feliciana married (2) MAJOR DIEGO RAMON Abt. 1676, son of JOSEPH DE MORALES-Y-RAMON and CATARINA MARTINEZ-GUAJARDO. He was born 1641 in Queretaro, Queretaro, Mexico, and died April 10, 1719 in San Juan Bautista del Rio Grande, Pre
2 CONC sido del Norte, Coahulia,Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the natural born son of Sgt. Major Joseph Ramon and Dona Catalina Martinez.
2 CONT
2 CONT His relationship with Maria de los Rios and their children are noted - the Handbook of Texas Online.
2 CONT
2 CONT Located in the state of Coahuila, Mexico, he owned the Hacienda named "El Carrizalejo",
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1674, he was a soldier with Francisco Elizondo's Expedition.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1688, he accompanied Governor Alonso De Leon into Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Between March 1691 to June 1698, he served as the third governor of Coahuila, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT On December 14, 1698, Diego Ramon and Fray Cristobal Montes de Oca founded the mission San Francisco Xavier y Valle de San Cristobal, some forty leaugues northeast of Villa de Pilon (Monclova).
2 CONT
2 CONT On March 1, 1700, he founded the Mission San Fernando Solano. This mission would later be relocated and remembered today as the Alamo.
2 CONT
2 CONT By March 28, 1701 Captain Ramon was receiving five hundred pesos for evey year served. Considered top paid in those years. From 1703, till his death, he was the Commandant of the Royal presidio of San Juan Bautista, Coahuila, Mexi
2 CONC co. This presidio had been established in 1702. His offical title was, Theniente General, Cabo y Caudillo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:From the book's
2 CONT
2 CONT Gallant Outcast - Texas Turmoil 1519-1734 by Ben Cuellar Ximenez. 
2 CONT
2 CONT San Juan Bautista, Gateway to Spanish Texas by Robert S. Weddle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Origen de los Fundadores de Texas, Nuevo Mexico, Coahilia, y Nuevo Leon, by Guillermo Garmendia Leal. Page 70.
2 CONT
2 CONT With All Arms by Carl Laurence Duaine. Page 242.
2 CONT
2 CONT With Makers of San Antonio by Frederick C. Chabot. Page 46.
2 CONT
2 CONT Northern New Spain, A Research Guide, by Thomas C. Barnes, Thomas H. Nayor and Charles W. Polzer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Diary of the Alarcon Expedition into Texas, 1718-1719 by Fray Francisco Celiz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published by the Quivira Society.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following is from "The Biographical Dictionary of Saltillo" by Martha Duron Jimenez and Ignacio Etchegaray, pg 143. Don Jose Ramon is mentioned as the eldest and the natural born son of Captain Diego Ramon.
2 CONT
2 CONT "En los ultimos dias del mes de abril de ese ano (1719), dejo de existir en el Presidio de Rio Grande el Capitan Diego Ramon, que tan importantes servicios presto en la conquista y pacificacion de la Provincia de Coahuila. Sus pad
2 CONC res fueron Don Josephe Ramon y Dona Andrea de los Rios, espanoles de nacimiento, pero que en 1636 se embarcaron para America yendo a residir primero en Cadereyta, y despues a la Villa del Saltillo de donde fue nombrado Procurador 
2 CONC General por recomendacion del Capitan Don Alonso de Leon de quien fue particular amigo. En esta villa nacio el ano de 1641 el tercero de sus hijos, que se llamo Diego y despues de recibir la education primaria que en esa epoca se 
2 CONC impartia, se dedico desde muy joven, a los trabajos del campo y a las campanas contra los indios, al lado de Don Alonso de Leon, el Capitan que lo llego a estima tanto coma a su padre, y que fue su gran maestro en la escuela de la
2 CONC s privaciones, fatigas y vicisitudes. Muerto el Capitan, su hijo Don Alonso que regreso de Espana a encargarse de la familia e intereses de su padre, continue sineto el amigo inseparabe de Diego Ramon....."
2 CONT
2 CONT El Capitan Diego Ramon contrajo matrimonio en el Presidio de San Francisco de Coahuila, con Dona Feliciana Camacho, de la que tuvo entre otros hijos a Don Jose que fue el mayor "
