2 CONT In 1540, they were residents of Santa Olalla, Spain, when their sons, don Francisco de Sosa Albornoz, a native of Toledo, Spain, and don Esteban de Sosa, came to Nueva Espana. 4 Don Francisco was successful in procuring matrimony 
2 CONC with dona Inez de Tapia y Sosa, daughter of the highly esteemed and remarkable conquistador Maese de Campo y Teniente don Andres de Tapia. Don Francisco and dona Inez became the parents of don Alonso de Sosa Albornoz, a native of 
2 CONC Mexico City born circa 1550, who eventually joined Onate’s colonizing expedition. 5
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.	Francisco SOSA ALBORNOZ m. 1560, Ines TAPIA SOSA, (daughter of Andres DE-TAPIA and Isabel DE-SOSA).
2 CONT * 1.	Alonso SOSA ALBORNOZ b. 1549, Xochitla, Mex, Mex, m. (1) abt 1565, Juana RAMIREZ ORTIZ, b. abt 1550, (daughter of Gabriel RAMIREZ and __________ ORTIZ) m. (2) 1585, Beatriz NAVARRO RODRIGUEZ, b. abt 1564, (daughter of Juan NA
2 CONC VARRO and Maria RODRIGUEZ SOSA). Alonso died abt 1601.
2 CONT
