1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Information by Joseph H. Sanchez, 10th great grandson
2 CONT
2 CONT According to other sites he was 53 when he married into the influential family of his wife, whose family was one of the most influential settlers of Monterrey in the Kingdom of Nueva Leon. She later remarried and had a large famil
2 CONC y. They seem to have had only the one son, who later came to New Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT He must have been a very influential person in his own right to marry into such a family.I have seen other sites
2 CONT give him the title "Conquistador". His story seems lost to time. Does anyone have any information on him?
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a lot older than Leanor, did he die and she remarried. I would like to know how and who made the connection of this family in New Mexico with the powerful families in Monterrey in the Kingdom of Nuevo Leon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Several ancestry sites show these two as the mother and father of Jose Tellez Giron, but I have not been able to establish the relation thru legal documents, etc. This link is crucial for linking the family to the families of Mont
2 CONC errey in Nueva Leon of the 1600's. We are related thru other individuals but this relation really hits the jackpot! 
