2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Name: Giovani Bautista Schiapapria, 
2 CONT *b. Bef 16 Nov 1627, d. 20 Apr 1695
2 CONT *Given Name: Juan Bautista Chapa
2 CONT *Event: Type: Immigration
2 CONT *Date: 1647
2 CONT *Place: New Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT CHAPA, JUAN BAUTISTA (1627-1695). Juan Bautista Chapa was born Giovanni Bautista Schiapapria in 1627 in Albisola, Italy, and is now recognized as the "anonymous historian" of Nuevo León, Mexico, where he arrived in the mid-sevente
2 CONC enth century and served Governor Alonso De León and other governors as their secretary for over four decades. Chapa knew these officials well, traveled through the province extensively, and wrote his observations of developments i
2 CONC n that far northern region in Historia del Nuevo Reino de León de 1650 a 1690. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The chapters of this work that treat Texas analyze the motives, frustrations, and strategies of Spanish expansion to the rim of the empire and constitute one of the most important primary sources for history in early Spanish Texas
2 CONC .qv The expeditions Chapa participated in include De León's first expedition in search of René Robert Cavelier, Sieur de La Salle's Texas colony, from Cadereyta to the mouth of the Rio Grande, and his second, which is generally su
2 CONC pposed to have reached Baffin Bay. Chapa also joined De León on his 1689 expeditions that found the ruins of La Salle's Fort St. Louis.
2 CONT
2 CONT His observations are particularly important because of the political impartiality he maintained by writing the book secretly and anonymously. He was a well-educated man who knew Italian (including the Genoese dialect), Spanish, La
2 CONC tin, and Tuscan. He left behind a perceptive and well-crafted historical work. The authorship of the Historia remained a mystery until 1961, when the edition published by the Biblioteca de Nuevo León revealed his identify.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chapa lived out his life in Nuevo León and married Beatriz Olivares de Treviño, daughter of one of Monterrey's elite families. They had four sons and two daughters. Chapa died in Nuevo León in 1695 and is recognized as the ancesto
2 CONC r of the very numerous Chapa families of northeastern Mexico and South Texas. Norman P. Brown has researched the Chapa descendants in Chapa: The First Four Generations, which covers the period from 1651 to 1800. Juan Bautista Chap
2 CONC a's own ancestors have been documented by Amancio J. Chapa, Jr., of La Joya, Texas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT BIBLIOGRAPHY: Robert S. Weddle, Wilderness Manhunt: The Spanish Search for La Salle (Austin: University of Texas Press, 1973). Eduardo J. Hinojosa
2 CONT
2 CONT The following descendent tree is found at the Corpus Christi Public Library.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHAPA
2 CONT
2 CONT THE FIRST FOUR GENERATIONS by NORMAN P. BROWN
2 CONT
2 CONT JUAN BAUTISTA SCHIAPAPRIA (CHAPA)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1627 - 1695
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Bautista Schiapapria (Chapa) was born in 1627 in Italy in Villa Albisola on the coast of Genoa, legitimate son of Bartholomé Schiapapria and Batistina Badi, daughter of Nicolas Badi. Juan Bautista was one of eight children:
2 CONT *1. Marietta - baptised in 1619
2 CONT *2. Nicolás - baptised in 1621
2 CONT *3. Juan Bautista - baptised in 1625
2 CONT *4. Juan Bautista - baptised Nov. 16, 1627
2 CONT *5. Francisco - baptised in 1632
2 CONT *6. Juan Francisco - baptised in 1633
2 CONT *7. Lucrecia - baptised in 1636
2 CONT *8. Lucrecia - baptised in 1637
2 CONT
2 CONT The surname in the above documents also appears as Schiappapietra. The family name was shortened to Chapa after Juan Bautista arrived in New Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1647 Juan Bautista left for New Spain. In 1653 he married Beatriz Olivares de Trevino, legitimate daughter of Juan Olivares and Juana de Treviño, at Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, and they had the following children:
2 CONT *I. Juan Bautista Chapa was born circa 1660 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon., resided in Villaldama around 1700, was mayor of Villaldama in 1705, and also is believed to be known as Juan de Chapa. Juan (Bautista) de Chapa married María de
2 CONC  Munguía on July 27, 1695, at the Metropolitan Chapel, Monterrey, Nuevo León. (M601491-0321) They had one son from this union:
2 CONT **A) Juan Joseph Chapa Munguía who was born March 24, 1710. (C601491-2104)
2 CONT *II. Nicolás Chapa married Inés Benavides Flores in 1710 and had six children:
2 CONT **A) José Florencio Chapa, born ca. 1714, married Margarita de la Peña and had the following children:
2 CONT ***1). Francisco Chapa who was 14 in 1753 and married María Rosalía López of Camargo.
2 CONT ***2). María Gertrudis Chapa who was 12 in 1753.
2 CONT ***3). Juan Chapa who was 10 in 1753.
2 CONT ***4). Gertrudis Chapa who was 8 in 1753 and married Juan Julian Gutiérrez.
2 CONT ***5). María Rosario Chapa who married José Antonio Ramos on June 11, 1776, at Mier, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT ***6). José Leonardo Chapa who died at 23 years of age on May 14, 1772.
2 CONT ***7). José Santiago Chapa who first married María Juana Hinojosa on January 22, 1777, at Mier, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT ***8). María Luisa Chapa who married José Antonio Guerra on Jan. 13, 1776 at Mier, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT ***9). Joaquín Chapa who married María Tomasa Báez de Benavides on February 13, 1776, at Guerrero, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT ***10) José Antonio Chapa who died at 18 years of age on March 21, 1772.
2 CONT **B) María Inés Chapa first married Juan Antonio Ruiz Garza. Her second marriage was to Manuel de Hinojosa. She had the following children:
2 CONT ***1). María Rosalía Hinojosa, who married José Ramon Guerra and died June 14, 1773, at Mier, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT ***2). María Gerarda Hinojosa who married José Miguel Sáenz on April 4, 1785, at Mier, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT ***3). Manuel Hinojosa, who was 19 in the Camargo census of May 31, 1750.
2 CONT **C) Antonia Chapa married José Salinas.
2 CONT **D) Clara María Chapa married Diego Longoria. They had the following children:
2 CONT ***1). Antonio Longoria who was born circa 1720.
2 CONT ***2). José Matías Longoria who married Margarita Hinojosa.
2 CONT ***3). Ana María Longoria who was born circa 1730.
2 CONT ***4). Juana Rosa Longoria who was born circa 1730.
2 CONT ***5). José Vincente Longoria who was born circa 1732.
2 CONT ***6). Juana Anastacia Longoria who was born circa 1732.
2 CONT ***7). Pedro Longoria who married Josefa Villarreal.
2 CONT ***8). Petra Longoria who was born circa 1734.
2 CONT **E) Miguel Eusebio Chapa married Ana María García. They had the following sons:
2 CONT ***1). Miguel Chapa who married Rosa María Treviño on August 15, 1764, at Camargo.
2 CONT ***2). Nicolas Chapa married Gertrudis Landa. Nicolas died on February 15, 1803, at Camargo.
2 CONT **F) Juan Bautista Chapa married Rita López de Jaen. They had at least five children:
2 CONT ***1). María Josefa Chapa who was 12 in 1753.
2 CONT ***2). María Gregoria Chapa who was 9 in 1753.
2 CONT ***3). José Francisco Chapa (6) who married María Agustina García 18 November, 1770, at Mier, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT ***4). María Antonia Gertrudis Chapa (3) who married José María Escobar Nov. 29, 1770, at Mier, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT ***5). María Ignacia Chapa who was 2 in 1753.
2 CONT *III. Gaspar Chapa was born in 1674 and died on January 8, 1694. He never married but lived in common law with María González and they had at least one child when Sergeant Gaspar Chapa was stationed in Saltillo, Coahuila:
2 CONT **A) Pedro Chapa married Josepha de las Casas on December 27, 1697, at the Metropolitan Chapel, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon. (M601497-0360) They had the following children:
2 CONT ***1). Juan Chapa Casas who was born April 28, 1698. (C601491-1227)
2 CONT ***2). Francisca María Chapa Casas who was born November 2, 1702. (C601491-1433)
2 CONT ***3). Lusgarda Chapa Casas who was born on July 2, 1705. (C601491-1615)
2 CONT **Pedro Chapa, widower of Josefha de las Casas, married Beatrix Rangel, both Spanish, May 10, 1711 in Saltillo, Coahuila.
2 CONT **Pedro Chapa, son of Gaspar Chapa amd María González, widower of Beatriz Rangel, married Catalina García, Spaniards, October 18, 1734 in Saltillo, Coahuila.
2 CONT *IV. José María Chapa was born ca. 1675. He married Nicolasa Fernández in 1694. On September 12, 1697, he married Josefa Sánchez de la Barrera. From his second marriage he had two children:
2 CONT **A) Agustín Xavier Chapa was born September 10, 1700 and married Antonia Guaxardo on February 4, 1727. They had the following children:
2 CONT ***1). María Gertrudes Chapa who was born July 31, 1729. (C601491-4097)
2 CONT ***2). Joseph Salbador Chapa who was born December 22, 1731. (C601492-0088)
2 CONT ***3). María Guadalupe Chapa who was born on May 16, 1732. (Montemorelos)
2 CONT ***4). María Eusebia Chapa who was born March 24, 1733. (C601492-0277)
2 CONT ***5). María Petra Chapa who was born July 18, 1735. (C601492-0619)
2 CONT ***6). Bisente Ferrer Chapa who was born February 5, 1737. (C601492-0861)
2 CONT ***7). Joseph Xavier Chapa who was born March 25, 1738. (C601492-1065)
2 CONT ***8). Anna María Chapa who was born March 2, 1739. (C601492-1252)
2 CONT ***9). Joseph Ramón Chapa who was born November 7, 1742. (C601492-1862)
2 CONT ***10) Joseph Francisco Chapa who was born May 25, 1744. (C601492-2164)
2 CONT ***11) Juana Josepha Chapa who was born June 18, 1747. (C601492-2705)
2 CONT ***12) Agustín Xavier Victorino Chapa who was born September 19, 1751. (C601492-3310)
2 CONT *Jose Maria Chapa married Maria Francisca de Ochoa in the Cathedral of Monterrey on June 27, 1717 (M601497-0767). There was one child of this union:
2 CONT **1). Maria Rosa Chapa was baptised on February 6, 1721, at the Cathedral of Monterrey (C601491-3216).
2 CONT **B) Josefa Chapa never married.
2 CONT *V. María Chapa married Francisco Alejo de Treviño. They had four Children:
2 CONT **A) Francisco Treviño married Clara Josefa de Cepeda.
2 CONT **B) Josefa Treviño married Bernabe Villarreal.
2 CONT **C) María Rosa Treviño who married Francisco Nuñez de Carvajal.
2 CONT **D) Pedro Regalado de Treviño.
2 CONT *VI. Juana Chapa is one about whom not much is known. (Ref: Protocoles of Monterrey, 1599-1700, 854, XXV, Exp. 1, Fol. 26, 14 Feb. 1687). Juana died November 8, 1709, at Monterrey. (12) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Bautista Chapa died April 20, 1695, in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon. Conquistador, discoverer, scrivener and author, his sixty-four years of life were adventuresome at a time when life was not easy. Juan Bautista was an intelligent,
2 CONC  valiant, and active person, having written a history of Nuevo Leon as well as participating in the Indian uprisings. He died a widower, poor and ailing, spending his last years in Cerralvo and Monterrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT LIST OF OTHERS USING THE CHAPA SURNAME
2 CONT
2 CONT Records show that servants often assumed the family name. These people are usually identified in the Spanish records as Mestizos, Mulatos, and Indios. Those of pure Spanish blood were noted as Españoles.
2 CONT *A) José Esteban Chapa was a household servant in the home of José Florencio Chapa who took the family name. He married María Juliana Gutiérrez in 1794.
2 CONT *B) Juan de Chapa and Maria Josepha (Indios) married in Saltillo, Coahuila, in 1719. (Saltillo Church Marriage Records).
2 CONT *C) Pedro Chapa Zalazar and Nicolaza de Torres, Mestizos, married June 27, 1709. (M601491-2041) They had the following daughter
2 CONT **1). Juana Xabiera Chapa who was born October 12, 1709. (C601491-2041)
2 CONT *Pedro Chapa Zalazar, son of Salvador de Olivares and Ysabel de Zalazar, married for a second time with Josepha de los Reyes on May 12, 1715. (M601497-0712)
2 CONT
2 CONT UNIDENTIFIED CHAPAS
2 CONT
2 CONT The following people with Chapa surnames are found in the Cadereyta records, but they have not been connected to any of the above known Chapas.
2 CONT *A) Tomás Francisco Javier Chapa married María Isabel de la Garza in Cadereyta on March 3, 1727. They had the following children:
2 CONT **1). José Antonio Chapa who married María Manuela Treviño on November 20, 1776, at Cadereyta.
2 CONT **2). Francisco Javier Chapa who married Ana Josefa Pérez on May 24, 1762 at Cadereyta.
2 CONT **3). María Apolinar Chapa who married Antonio Pérez on July 7, 1762 at Cadereyta.
2 CONT **4). Ana María Chapa married Miguel Treviño on May 27, 1772 at Cadereyta.
2 CONT *Francisco Chapa's second marriage was to Josepha de Torres on July 31, 1735. (M601266-0396)
2 CONT *B). Aparicio Chapa married Margarita Herrera. He was born circa 1739 in Cadereyta. They had one son:
2 CONT **1). Santiago Chapa married Jacinta Villarreal on August 30, 1759, at Cadereyta.
