2 CONT JUAN BAUTISTA SCHIAPAPRIA (CHAPA)
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Bautista Schiapapria (0100) was born in Villa Albisola on the coast of Italy and was baptized on November 16, 1627, the legitimate son of Bartholome Schiapapria and Batistina Badi. He left Italy in 1647 for New Spain. He marr
2 CONC ied Beatriz Olivares de Trevino in 1653. Beatriz was the legitimate daughter of Juan Olivares and Juana de Trevino.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Bautista Chapa (0100) was a conquistador, discoverer, and author. He served as secretary to the governors of Nuevo Leon and Coahuila. He died April 20, 1695, at Monterrey, Nuevo Leon.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Juan Bautista Chapa (0203), the younger, was born circa 1657 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, resided in Villaldama around 1700, was mayor of Villaldama in 1705, and also is believed to be known as Juan de Chapa. Juan (Bautista) de Cha
2 CONC pa married Maria de Munguia on July 27, 1695, at the Metropolitan Chapel, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon (M601491-0321). They had one son from this union. 2. Nicolas Chapa (0206) was born 1655 and married Ines Benavides Flores in 1710 and 
2 CONC had six children. 3. Gaspar Chapa (0202) died on January 8, 1694. He never married but lived in common law with Maria Gonzalez and they had at least one child. 4. Jose Maria Chapa (0200) was born circa 1663. He married Nicolasa Fe
2 CONC rnandez in 1694. On September 12, 1697, he married Josefa Sanchez de la Barrera. From his second marriage he had two children. He married Maria Francisca de Ochoa on June 27, 1717 at Monterrey, Nuevo Leon [M601497-0767]. There was
2 CONC  one child from the third marriage. 5. Maria Chapa (0204) married Alferez Real Francisco de Trevino. They had four children. Maria died before 1709. 6. Juana Chapa (0205) is one about whom not much is known. Juana is reported to h
2 CONC ave died on November 8, 1709, in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon. In her Testament she declared that she had three children out of wedlock. http://genforum.genealogy.com/longoria/messages/524.html
2 CONT
