2 CONT 1627 - 1695
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Bautista Schiapapria (Chapa) was born in 1627 in Italy in Villa Albisola on the coast of Genoa, legitimate son of Bartholomé Schiapapria and Batistina Badi, daughter of Nicolas Badi. Juan Bautista was one of eight children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Marietta - baptised in 1619 2. Nicolás - baptised in 1621 3. Juan Bautista - baptised in 1625 4. Juan Bautista - baptised Nov. 16, 1627 5. Francisco - baptised in 1632 6. Juan Francisco - baptised in 1633 7. Lucrecia - baptised
2 CONC  in 1636 8. Lucrecia - baptised in 1637 The surname in the above documents also appears as Schiappapietra. The family name was shortened to Chapa after Juan Bautista arrived in New Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1647 Juan Bautista left for New Spain. In 1653 he married Beatriz Olivares de Trevino, legitimate daughter of Juan Olivares and Juana de Treviño, at Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, and they had the following children:
2 CONT
