2 CONC n Bautista Chapa died April 20, 1695, in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon. Conquistador, discoverer, scrivener and author, his sixty-four years of life were adventuresome at a time when life was not easy. Juan Bautista was an intelligent, va
2 CONC liant, and active person, having written a history of Nuevo Leon as well as participating in the Indian uprisings. He died a widower, poor and ailing, spending his last years in Cerralvo and Monterrey.
