2 CONT The following people with Chapa surnames are found in the Cadereyta records, but they have not been connected to any of the above known Chapas.
2 CONT
2 CONT A) Tomás Francisco Javier Chapa married María Isabel de la Garza in Cadereyta on March 3, 1727. They had the following children: 1). José Antonio Chapa who married María Manuela Treviño on November 20, 1776, at Cadereyta. 2). Fran
2 CONC cisco Javier Chapa who married Ana Josefa Pérez on May 24, 1762 at Cadereyta. 3). María Apolinar Chapa who married Antonio Pérez on July 7, 1762 at Cadereyta. 4). Ana María Chapa married Miguel Treviño on May 27, 1772 at Cadereyta
2 CONC . Francisco Chapa's second marriage was to Josepha de Torres on July 31, 1735. (M601266-0396) B). Aparicio Chapa married Margarita Herrera. He was born circa 1739 in Cadereyta. They had one son: 1). Santiago Chapa married Jacinta 
2 CONC Villarreal on August 30, 1759, at Cadereyta. Bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Cavazos Garza, Israel, Catalogo y Sintesis de los Protocolos del Archivo Municipal de Monterrey, Publicaciones de Instituto Tecnologico y de Estudios Superiores de Monterrey, Monterrey, 1966 Vol. 1 1599 - 1700 Pub. 1966, Vol. 2
2 CONC  1700 - 1726, Vol. 3 1726 - 1756 Pub. 1986, Vol. 4 1756 - 1785 Pub. 1988, Vol. 5 1785 - 1795 Pub. 1988 2. Cavazos Garza, Israel, Cedulario Autobiografico de Pobladores Y Conquistadores de Nuevo Leon, UANL, Monterrey, 1964 3. Cavaz
2 CONC os Garza, Israel, Diccionario Biografico de Nuevo Leon, Tomo 1, UANL, Monterrey, 1984 4. Cavazos Garza, Israel, El Cronista Anonimo, A.G.E.N.L., Monterrey, 1988 5. Duaine Carl L., Caverns of Oblivion, Packrat Press, Manchaca, Texa
2 CONC s, 1971 6. Gonzales de la Garza, Rodolfo, Apellidos de Tamp., - N. Leon, Coah. Y Texas, Privately Published, N. Laredo, Tamps., Mexico, 1980 7. Guerra, Antonio Maria, Mier en la Historia, 1953 8. Herrera Perez, Octavio, Anales y T
2 CONC estimonios del Cantaro, Cd. Victoria, Tam., 1986 9. Hinojosa, Nick, Private papers on the Hinojosa surname 10. Mendirichaga Cueva, Tomas, Origin of the Surnames Garza Y Trevino in Nuevo Leon, Editorial Jus, S. A., Mexico, 1982, tr
2 CONC anslated by Edna G. Brown, 1989. 11. Mormon Microfilm Reels for Births, Marriages, and Deaths at: Cadereyta, Nuevo Leon Guerrero, Tamaulipas Camargo, Tamaulipas Mier, Tamaulipas Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon Monterrey, Nuevo Leon 12. Quiño
2 CONC nes, Jr., Manuel. Research notes on the parrochial records of Saltillo, Coahuila. 13. Seabury, Frances William, "Seabury Papers", Barker Texas History Center, University of Texas at Austin 14. Scott, Florence Johnson, Historical H
2 CONC eritage of the Lower Rio Grande, La Retama Press, Rio Grande City, Texas, Second Printing of 1937 Edition, 1970 15. Garmendia Leal, Guillermo, Origin de los Fundadores de Tamaulipas "Cerralvo", Privately Printed, 1993. The Handboo
2 CONC k of Texas Online is a joint project of The General Libraries at the University of Texas at Austin and the Texas State Historical Association .
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT A.K.A. Juan Bautista Chapa. His Italian surname was shorten to the surname, Chapa. He is the ancestor of the Chapa family in the New World. He arrived in New Spain in 1647. On January 1694, he prepared his will, and died the follo
2 CONC wing year. See Texas & Northeastern Mexico, 1630-1690, by Juan Bautista Chapa, edited by William C.Foster.
