1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 3. Gaspar Chapa (0202) died on January 8, 1694. He never married but lived in common law with Maria Gonzalez and they had at least one child.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gaspar Chapa (0202) was the legitimate son of Juan Bautista Chapa (0100) and Beatriz Olivares de Trevino. Gaspar died on January 8, 1694. He never married but lived in common law with Maria Gonzalez and they had at least one child
2 CONC .
2 CONT *1. Pedro Chapa (0330) 
2 CONT **married Josefa de las Casas on December 27, 1697, at the Metropolitan Chapel, Monterrey, Nuevo Leon. [M601497-0360] They had three children. 
2 CONT **Pedro Chapa (0330), widower of Josefa de las Casas, married Beatrix Rangel, both Spanish, May 10, 1711, in Saltillo, Coahuila. 
2 CONT **Pedro Chapa (0330), son of Gaspar Chapa (0202) and Maria Gonzalez, widower of Beatriz Rangel, married Catalina Garcia, Spaniards, October 18, 1734 in Saltillo, Coahuila.
2 CONT
