1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mariana Saucedo was born sometime around 1680 in or near the town of Saltillo to Mateo Saucedo and Maria Perez according to the marriage record in 1704.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariana was said to have been originaly from the vecinity of Saltillo where she would marry a man named Sebastián de Ansaldo, who travelled from Guadalajara, Jalisco to the north in search for opportunity out on the frontier. Salt
2 CONC illo at the time was growing to become a commercial center connecting the regions of central Mexico with the northern frontier in Coahuila and Nuevo Leon. The motive of this move from Guadalajara may be due to the prospect of land
2 CONC  out on the frontier as a result.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariana's parents were said to have both been Castizos, meaning that both of her parents had 3/4 Spaniard and 1/4 Indigenous ancestry. This means that it is probable that Mariana had at least two great grandparents who were Indige
2 CONC nous.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is not known from where her recent Indigenous ancestry came from, but it is most likely that her Indigenous ancestors were originally from groups inhabiting central Mexico in modern-day Zacatecas, San Luis Potosí, or Guanajato.
2 CONC  It is also possible that they could have originated from even more down south but where they came from is not known truly at the moment.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is unknown when Mariana passed away. Perhaps in the mid-18th century in Nuevo Leon. It is a possibility that she passed away in Cerralvo given that her daughter Ana Maria Anzaldua was said to have been from there in her death r
2 CONC ecord in 1790.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT -Transcription written by Moises Garza-
2 CONT
2 CONT "En veinte y dos dias del mes de Disiembre de setecinetos, y cuatro as, en Villa de Santiago, del Saltillo, abiendo presedido ynformacion de libertad, y solturas y publicaciones de vanas, en tres dias festivos intermisaruz solemni
2 CONC a qe lo fueron la primera, Domingo siete, la segunda lunes, ocho, y la tercera Domingo Catorce del mes de Diciembre de setecinetos y quatro as. Case a Sebastian de Ansaldo orig nario de la ciudad de Guadalaxa. y vesino de esta va.
2 CONC  hijo lex de D Jan. de Ansaldo, y de Catarina, de Dueñas Vidarte veci nos de dicha ciudad, Con Mariana Saucedo, hija lexma. de Mateo Saucedo, y de Maria Peres, casrisos, vecinos deesta Va. fueron sus pad nos. Alonso de Sepeda, y M
2 CONC aria de Sepeda su hermana es panoles y vecinos desta dicha Villa, y testigos al berlos cas al Cappn. Jua de la Pena, el Cappn. Diego Rodriguez, i otra mucha pte. y pa qe conste lo firme ficha ut supra"
2 CONT
2 CONT Website URL: [https://www.wearecousins.info/2018/11/1704-marriage-of-sebastian-ansaldua-and-mariana-sauceda/]
