1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 22. Pedro4 Longoria Chapa (Clara3 Chapa Benavides, Nicolas2 Chapa Treviño, Juan Bautista Schiapapria1 Chapa) 
2 CONT *was born Abt 1732 in Cerralvo , and died in Camargo, Tamaulipas. 
2 CONT *He married Maria Josefa Villarreal Hinojosa Abt 1758 in Camargo, Tamaulipas, 
2 CONT **daughter of Juan Villarreal Oropeza and Maria Hinojosa Garza.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Pedro Longoria Chapa and Maria Villarreal Hinojosa are:
2 CONT *1. + 47 i. Pedro5 Longoria Villarreal, 
2 CONT **born Abt 1766 in Camargo, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT *2. 48 ii. Rafael Longoria Villarreal, 
2 CONT **born Abt 1768 in Camargo, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT *3. 49 iii. Josefa Longoria Villarreal, 
2 CONT **born Abt 1772 in Camargo, Tamaulipas; 
2 CONT **died August 08, 1802 in Matamoros, Tamaulipas. 
2 CONT **She married Patricio Leal November 02, 1788 in Camargo, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT *4. 50 iv. Santiago Longoria Villarreal, 
2 CONT **born Abt 1773 in Camargo, Tamaulipas; 
2 CONT **died in Matamoros, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT *5. 51 v. Leocadia Longoria Villarreal, 
2 CONT **born Abt 1774 in Camargo, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://longoriaf.tripod.com/Chapa.htm#Generation No. 19911
2 CONT
2 CONT ==================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedro LONGORIA Chapa [209] 
2 CONT *was born about 1733 in Cerralvo, Nuevo Leon, New Spain. 
2 CONT *He died by 1772 at the age of 39.[2429],[2430] 
2 CONT *He was a Rancher in La Grulla, Starr County, Texas, New Spain. Pedro Longoria was the Original Grantee of Porcion 94, Camargo. 
2 CONT *Parents: Juan Diego LONGORIA Garcia and Maria Clara de CHAPA.
2 CONT *Spouse: Maria Josefa VILLARREAL. Maria Josefa VILLARREAL and Pedro LONGORIA Chapa were married in 1755.[430] Pedro is not listed by name in the Camargo Census of July 12, 1757; therefore I suspect he was married sometime after Ju
2 CONC ly 1757. Children were: 
2 CONT **1. Jose Rafael LONGORIA Villarreal, 
2 CONT **2. Santiago LONGORIA Villarreal, 
2 CONT **3. Josefa LONGORIA Villarreal, 
2 CONT **4. Maria Leocadia LONGORIA Villarreal, 
2 CONT **5. Pedro Jose LONGORIA Villarreal.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b144.html#P20
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Pedro Longoria was the Original Grantee of a land grant from the King of Spain in 1767.  The land grant was identified as Porcion 94, in the jurisdiction of the Municipality of Camargo, and is located on the left (north) side of t
2 CONC he Rio Grande River in what is now the state of Texas.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT In 1767, he received from the King of Spain, the land grants of Porcion 94 (4,650 acres). Today this ranch is known as the Santa Rita Ranch in Brooks County, Texas.
