1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Los Origens De La Familia Olivares by Zacarias Joel Olivarez (webcached 2/2/2013):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/o/l/i/Zacarias--J-Olivarez/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0035.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrudis Estefana Longoria (b. Abt. 1735, d. Abt. 1817)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrudis Estefana Longoria 
2 CONT *(daughter of Cpt. Juan Diego Longoria Garcia and Maria Chapa Baez Benavidez) was born Abt. 1735 in Seville Spain (sic), and 
2 CONT *died Abt. 1817 in Rancho La Bonita near Camargo Mexico. 
2 CONT *She married (1) Tomas De Olivares on Abt. 1758 in Camargo Mexico, 
2 CONT **son of Blas De Olivares and Maria Ramona Escandon. 
2 CONT *She married (2) Miguel Lopez De Jaen on Abt. 1758 in Camargo Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrudis Longoria was married to Miguel Lopez De Jaen before she married Tomas De Olivares. Their marriage record can be found on www.familysearch.org Batch Number 0760051. Miguel Lopez De Jaen was born in Seville Spain as was Ge
2 CONC rtrudis Longoria (sic). They came to New Spain in late 1746 to acquire land from the King of Spain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They migrated from El Nuevo Reino De Leon with the Jose Escandon Expedition under the command of Captain Blas Maria de La Garza, and were originators of the town of Nuestra Senora de Santa Ana de Camargo. Today, this town is just 
2 CONC called Camargo Mexico, and it is just across the border from Rio Grande City (RGC) Texas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrudis and her first husband Miguel Lopez De Jaen can be found in the 1750 Census for Camargo which lists all the families that were original settlers of Camargo.Miguel Lopez de Jaen died between 1750 and 1757 since in the 1757
2 CONC  Census, Gertrudis is listed as a widow. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Shortly after 1757, she met Don Tomas de Olivares and married him.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Gertrudis Estefana Longoria:
2 CONT *Date born 2: 1735, Cerralvo
2 CONT *Died 2: 10 Feb 1810, Camargo, NL, Mexico.80
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Gertrudis Estefana Longoria and Tomas De Olivares:
2 CONT *Marriage: Abt. 1758, Camargo Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Gertrudis Estefana Longoria and Tomas De Olivares are:
2 CONT *1. +Francisco Jose De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1765, Rancho La Bonita near Camargo Mx., 
2 CONT **d. date unknown.
2 CONT *2. +Maria Gertrudis De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. 13 Jul 1767, Rancho La Bonita near Camargo Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1795, Camargo Mexico.
2 CONT *3. +Alejandro De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1772, Rancho La Bonita near Camargo Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1840, Rancho La Bonita Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Gertrudis Estefana Longoria and Miguel Lopez De Jaen are:
2 CONT *1. Jose Cayetano Lopez De Jaen, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1745, Sevilla Spain, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1805, Camargo Mexico.
2 CONT *2. Maria Gertrudis Lopez De Jaen, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1746, Sevilla Spain, 
2 CONT **d. date unknown, ABT 1800.
2 CONT *3. Jose Miguel Lopez De Jaen II, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1748, Camargo Mexico
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes: There are problems with the assertion that Gertrudis was born in Spain. Her parents' families, for instance, were long settled in New Spain, and no documented journey has been identified in any record. Nonethel
2 CONC ess, the two births in Sevilla (presuming she did in fact give birth at ages 10 and 11) would indicate that their mother came from Andalucia. (Also noted, there is no definite information on her first husband Miguel's birth locati
2 CONC on.)
2 CONT
2 CONT For the time being, I'm going on the idea that she was born in New Spain, and that Miguel was born on the Peninsula, and that the Spanish births (all of which carry only the father's apellido) were probably from an earlier marriag
2 CONC e.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT (Research):She is listed as a widow in the July 12, 1757 Census of Camargo, Tamaulipas, México.
