1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Santiago LONGORIA Villarreal209 was born (date unknown). Santiago sold his interest in Porcion 94 to his brother Pedro by deed in the Archives of Camargo, according to Seabury. This is confirmed by a handwritten no
2 CONC te left by my grandfather, Eugenio Longoria, which noted that Santiago sold his interest in the Porcion to his brother Pedro. Parents: Pedro LONGORIA Chapa and Maria Josefa VILLARREAL.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b146.html#P2302
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Joseph Santiago LONGORIA1453,2339 was born (date unknown). Santiago Longoria was the Original Grantee of Porcion 4 in Camargo (on the south side of the Rio Grande). Seabury indicates that there is a sale deed in the Archives of Ca
2 CONC margo, whereby Santiago sold his interest (in Porcion 94?) to Pedro Longoria, the father of Juan Santiago Longoria. I believe Seabury has confused two different men by the name of Santiago Longoria. The Santiago who married Ana de
2 CONC  Hinojosa was the Original Grantee of Porcion 4. The Santiago who sold his interest in Porcion 94 to his brother Pedro was not the same as the Original Grantee of Porcion 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT I believe this may be the same Santiago Longoria who was one of the 13 original founders in 1774 of the "congregacion" named San Juan de los Esteros Hermosos about 20 miles upstream from the mouth of the Rio Grande River; the "con
2 CONC gregacion" grew into the city known today as Matamoros, Tamaulipas, Mexico. That Santiago was married to Maria Hinojosa, and as I note for Ana de Hinojosa she was sometimes referred to as Anna Maria de Hinojosa. The ranch they fou
2 CONC nded near Matamoros was named Longoreño. Parents: Joseph LONGORIA Garcia and Maria CHAPA Benavides.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Ana de HINOJOSA. Ana de HINOJOSA and Joseph Santiago LONGORIA were married. Children were: Alejandro LONGORIA, Francisca LONGORIA, Maria de Jesus LONGORIA, Jose Vidal LONGORIA, Juan Jose LONGORIA, Maria Rita LONGORIA, Juli
2 CONC an LONGORIA, Luis LONGORIA.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b136.html#P382
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 14. Joseph Santiago4 Longoria (Maria3 Chapa Benavides, Nicolas2 Chapa Treviño, Juan Bautista Schiapapria1 Chapa) was born Abt 1730 in Cerralvo , and died Abt 1820 in Matamoros, Tamaulipas. He married Ana Maria Hinojosa Abt 1760 in
2 CONC  Cerralvo , daughter of Bernardo Hinojosa and Nicolasa Rendon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joseph Longoria and Ana Hinojosa are:
2 CONT
2 CONT + 31 i. Alejandro5 Longoria Hinojosa, born January 1756 in Camargo, Tamaulipas; died October 15, 1828 in Matamoros, Tamaulipas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT + 32 ii. Julian Longoria Hinojosa, born Abt January 1762 in Camargo, Tamaulipas; died in Matamoros, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT
2 CONT 33 iii. M® de Jesus Longoria Hinojosa, born Abt January 1763 in Camargo, Tamaulipas; died in Matamoros, Tamaulipas. She married José Flores Galan October 27, 1792 in Camargo, Tamaulipas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 34 iv. Vital Longoria Hinojosa, born January 1765 in Camargo, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT
2 CONT 35 v. Rita Longoria Hinojosa, born Abt 1773 in Camargo, Tamaulipas; died in Matamoros, Tamaulipas. She married Antonio Flores April 16, 1798 in Camargo, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT
2 CONT 36 vi. Francisca Longoria Hinojosa, born Abt January 1779 in Camargo, Tamaulipas; died in Matamoros, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT
2 CONT 37 vii. Luis Longoria Hinojosa, born Abt 1780 in Camargo, Tamaulipas; died June 06, 1784 in Camargo, Tamaulipas.
2 CONT
2 CONT 38 viii. Juan José Longoria Hinojosa, born Abt 1788 in Camargo, Tamaulipas; died August 08, 1789.
2 CONT
