2 CONT 21. CATALINA5 DE URIBE-TREVINO (PHELIPE4 DE URIBE-DE-LA-CADENA-LOBO, ANTONIO3 URIBE-DE-LA-CADENA-VERGARA, JOSE2 URIBE-Y-VERGARA-TOVAR, PEDRO1 URIBE-Y-VERGARA) was born Bet. 1708 - 1709. She married CAPTAIN TOMAS-TADEO SANCHEZ-DE-L
2 CONC A-BARRERA April 11, 1729 in Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico, son of TOMAS SANCHEZ-DE-LA-BARRERA and MARIA-JOSEFA DE-LA-GARZA-SOSA. He was born June 04, 1709 in Cienega de Flores, Nuevo Leon, Mexico, and died January 21, 1796 in Lare
2 CONC do, Webb County, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for CAPTAIN TOMAS-TADEO SANCHEZ-DE-LA-BARRERA:
2 CONT
2 CONT In the book, Mil Familias III, by Rodolfo Gonzalez de la Garza, he is listed as a descendent of the Don Alonso of Estrada, Duke of Aragon, Royal Treasurer and Governor of New Spain, (Mexico).
2 CONT
2 CONT He is also a descendent of the Onate-Zaldivar Family of Zacatecas and New Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 15, 1755, he founded the town of San Agustin de Laredo (Laredo Texas).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1767 he received a royal charter (Porcion 10 & 11) from the king of Spain. A Total of 10,628 acres located in Webb County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Ranches and Ranching in Spanish Texas by Lyle W. Williams. Page 8
2 CONT
2 CONT Handbook on Texas Online.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and his family are listed on the July 22, 1757 census for Laredo, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Webb County Family Histories Volume I, Page 233.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes for CATALINA DE URIBE-TREVINO and TOMAS-TADEO SANCHEZ-DE-LA-BARRERA:
2 CONT
