1 NOTE {geni:about_me} María Navarra Died 21 February 1694 - Monterrey, Nuevo León, México
2 CONT  •Buried - Parroquia del Sagrario - Monterrey, Nuevo León, México
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse(s) and child(ren)
2 CONT  ?Married to Pedro Navarra, ¦Juan Navarro Navarra
2 CONT
2 CONT http://gw5.geneanet.org/sanchiz?lang=en;pz=tomas;nz=sanchez+garza;ocz=0;p=maria;n=navarra
2 CONT =====================
2 CONT A  pedigree presented here of   http://www.vsalgs.org/stnemgenealogy/BernardoGutierrez.pdf   of Maria RODRIGUEZ SOSA daughter of  Baltazar DE-SOSA  is as follows 
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatriz NAVARRO RODRIGUEZ b. abt. 1570 d. bef. 1626 married  Bernabe DE-LAS-CASAS LOPEZ b. abt. 1573 m. abt. 1602 d. 1632   daugher of   
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria RODRIGUEZ SOSA married  Juan NAVARRO SOSA b. 1533 m. abt. 1559 d. 1594 daughter of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Baltazar DE-SOSA  married  Maria Ines RODRIGUEZ MONTEMAYOR  b. abt. 1549 daughter of  
2 CONT
2 CONT Gobernador Diego DE-MONTEMAYOR HERNANDEZ b. abt. 1530 m. abt. 1548 d. abt. 1610 married  Ines RODRIGUEZ b. abt. 1531 son of
2 CONT
2 CONT  Juan DE-MONTEMAYOR married  Mayor HERNANDEZ
2 CONT
2 CONT to me this  indicates that her being the daughter of Baltazar DE-SOSA is questionable
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The surname is a place name, indicating her birthplace. This was a custom adopted by Jewish and/or convesos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sanchez has been listed as her surname on other trees, but there is no documentation to prove this.
2 CONT
2 CONT In my tree there is another Maria de Navarra who was born in Navarra, c. 1400.  They are not the same person. (Obviously)
