1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cavazos Garza, Israel.  ''Catálogo y Síntesis de los Protocolos del Archivo Municipal de Monterrey 1599-1700'', Instituto Tecnologico y de Estudios Superiores de Monterrey, Monterrey, Nuevo León, México, 1966, page
2 CONC s 142-143, #456 [V, fol. 170v., no.92].  ...  This protocolo sets forth the '''will of Capitán Francisco Botello de Morales'''.  He states that he's the legitimate son of '''Pedro Botello de Morales''' and Ama María de Avila, both
2 CONC  deceased and that his father was a '''native of Valverde, Extremadura, Spain''', and that his mother was a native of the city of Códova, Spain.  He stipulates burial in the "Parroquial, then sets forth his debts.  He states that 
2 CONC he married Juana de la Garza, legitimate daughter of Marcos Alonso de la Garza and Catalina Martínez Guajardo, who were residents of Saltillo. He identifies his children Sebastián, María, Diego, Melchora, Pedro, Petrona, Juan, and
2 CONC  Francisca--all adults. Then he allocates inheritances and states that María will marry José de la Serna, Melchora is to marry Andrés González, Petronila to marry Diego Galván, and Francisca now married to Juan Bautista de Saldúa,
2 CONC   ...  '''Monterrey, 16 April 1696''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''______________________________'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Pedro BOTELLO DE MORALES384,640 was born (date unknown). On the bottom of page 246 of "Index to the Marriage Investigations of the Diocese of Guadalajara" the editors identify Pedro Botello de Morales and Ana Maria de Avila 
2 CONC as the parents of Francisco Botello de Morales. The editors also state that Francisco Botello de Morales was married twice: (1) to Juana de la Garza, and (2) Catalina Martinez Guajardo. I have found no information to verify the se
2 CONC cond marriage and note that Catalina Martinez Guajardo was the name of Juana de la Garza's mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Ana Maria de AVILA. Ana Maria de AVILA and Capt. Pedro BOTELLO DE MORALES385 were married. I believe this is the same Pedro Botello de Morales noted in a census of the Villa of Cerralvo (Monterrey) conducted on September 4
2 CONC , 1626, which stated that Pedro Botello de Morales, his wife and children lived in a jacal located behind the house owned by Blas de la Garza and Alonso de Treviño. The jacal was constructed of "carrizo cubierto con zacate", that 
2 CONC is of reeds covered with grass. Children were: Captain Francisco BOTELLO DE MORALES, Melchora BOTELLO DE MORALES (aka Juana Botello de Morales).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b25.html#P8661
2 CONT
2 CONT ===================
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendents of Captain Pedro Botello de Morales
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. CAPTAIN PEDRO3 BOTELLO-DE-MORALES (BUENTELLO-GUERRERO, BOTELLO1 BUENTELLO) was born 1581 in Villa de Valverde, Extremadura, Spain, and died 1696. He married (1) Dona ANA-MARIA DE AVILA 1608 in Cordoba, Spain. She was born in Co
2 CONC rdoba, Spain, and died 1696. He met (2) UNKNOWN NAME 1615. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.somosprimos.com/inclan/botello.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
