2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "De este mismo puesto como dos leguas está una estancia cuyo nombre es la Cuevas, y es el dueño de esta estancia una mujer española llamada Melchora de los Reyes, viuda, mujer que fue de Luis Delgadillo.  Está en las orillas d
2 CONC e un arroyo este puesto de muy poca agua zarca.  Críase en esta estancia gandados mayores y caballada.  Tiene por hijos 5 varones 4 hijas."
2 CONT 	So: In her first marriage, to Rodrigo de Carbajal, with residence in Ahuacatlán, Nayarit, she begat three children during the first few years of the 1600s: Rodrigo de Carbajal y Ulloa, Juan Rodríguez de Carbajal and Elvira de C
2 CONC arbajal y Ulloa (talked about in previous correspondence).
2 CONT 	In her second wedlock, to Luis Delgadillo, were born:
2 CONT 	1.  The priest, Luis Delgadillo or Luis de Frías, who died 2 June 1637 and was buried in Mexticacán.
2 CONT 	2.  Your ancestor, Juan Pérez de Frías, who married Mariana López.
2 CONT 	3.  María Delgadillo, married to N.N.  The mother of Melchora de los Reyes, married 16 Apr 1654 in Nochistlán to Nicolás Vargas and Diego Pérez Delgadillo or Pérez de Frías married 26 Jan 1656 to Catalina Cortés de Isla.  
2 CONC MD 7 May 1718 (6119) has the latter two as brother and sister.
2 CONT 	4.  Hernando Delgadillo, married to Andrea de Rodas.
2 CONT 	5.  Josefa Delgadillo, wed to Francisco Morgado on 13 Jan 1655.
2 CONT 	I believe Luis Delgadillo was a brother of Diego Delgadillo, Isabel Calderón's first husband, and of Juan Rodríguez de Frías, the three sons of Hernando de Frías.
2 CONT 	In his will, in Aguascalientes, 2 Nov 1679, Alvaro Marín de Peñalosa states that before his second marriage to Petrona de Sotomayor, two daughters were born and he  recognizes them.  Petrona, or Petronila, was your ancestor Ele
2 CONC na's sister and I sent you her first marriage record in Sierra de Pinos.  Says the will:
2 CONT 	"Soi casado y velado...con Petrona de Sotomayor...hija legítima de Juan de Montañez y de María de la Ruela vecinos de los Pinos...ubimos y procreamos por nuestros hijos legítimos a Agustín Marín y a Andrés Marín y antes d
2 CONC e dicho matrimonio tube en la dicha Petrona Sotomayor mi mujer a Antonia Marín y a Teresa Marín mis hijas y por tales las reconozco y legítimo."
2 CONT 	Alvaro states that he was born in Teocaltiche and his parents were Juan Marín de Peñalosa and María de Sandi, residents of that township.  His first wife was Isabel de Mayorga.
2 CONT 	In his will dated 15 Mar 1671, Juan de Luévana, a son of Juan de Luévana and María López de Elizalde, married María de Alvarado, whose parents were Pedro de Alvarado and Magdalena de Frías.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.	a Marriage 13 Jun 1674 "en el Rancho de la Cueva de Juan de Carbajal," between: Juan de Carbajal, español, hijo de Rodrigo de Carbajal y Melchora de los Reyes, difuntos, natural de Aguacatlán en este obispado; Ana María, ind
2 CONC ia del pueblo de Toyagua, viuda de Juan Bartolomé, indio.  (The town of Toyagua is in Zacatecas.)
