1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 7. 2ND DUKE OF FRIAS INIGO7 FERNANDEZ-DE-VELASCO (PEDRO6, PEDRO5, JUAN4, PEDRO3, FERNAN2 SANCHEZ-DE-VELASCO, SANCHO1) was born Abt. 1460, and died 17 Oct 1528. He married MARQUESES MARIA DE TOVAR-Y-VIVERO 1480, dau
2 CONC ghter of LUIS DE TOVAR and MARIA DE VIVERO-Y-SOTOMAYOR. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for 2ND DUKE OF FRIAS INIGO FERNANDEZ-DE-VELASCO: 2nd Duke of Frias, 4th Count of Haro
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for MARQUESES MARIA DE TOVAR-Y-VIVERO: 1st Marqueses de Berlanga.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of INIGO FERNANDEZ-DE-VELASCO and MARIA DE TOVAR-Y-VIVERO are:
2 CONT * i. 3RD DUKE OF FRIAS PEDRO8 FERNANDEZ-DE-VELASCO, d. 10 Nov 1559; m. JULIANA-ANGELA DE VELASCO-Y-ARAGON.
2 CONT * 15. ii. 1ST MARQUEZ OF BERLANGA JUAN DE VELASCO-Y-TOVAR.
2 CONT * 16. iii. ISABEL DE VELASCO.
2 CONT * iv. INIGO FERNANDEZ-DE-VELASCO-Y-TOVAR.Notes for INIGO FERNANDEZ-DE-VELASCO-Y-TOVAR:On November 15, 1647, he served as Governor of Milan.
2 CONT * v. BERNARDINO FERNANDEZ-DE-VELASCO-Y-TOVAR.Notes for BERNARDINO FERNANDEZ-DE-VELASCO-Y-TOVAR:On Febuary 24, 1646, he served as Governor of Milan.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.somosprimos.com/inclan/velasco.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%8D%C3%B1igo_Fern%C3%A1ndez_de_Velasco,_2nd_Duke_of_Fr%C3%ADas
2 CONT
2 CONT Íñigo Fernández de Velasco, 2nd Duke of Frías, Grandee of Spain, (in full, Spanish: Don Íñigo Fernández de Velasco y López de Mendoza, segundo duque de la villa de Frías, cuarto conde de Haro, octavo Condestable de Castilla, mayor
2 CONC azgo y señor de la Casa de Velasco, Caballero del Toisón de Oro), (1462–17 September 1528), was a Spanish nobleman and Duke of Frias.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fernández de Velasco was the son of Pedro Fernández de Velasco and of Mencía de Mendoza y Figueroa, and he inherited the titles from his older brother Bernardino, who had no legitimate male issue. He married María de Tovar, Lady o
2 CONC f Berlanga, with whom he had six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Pedro Fernández de Velasco, 3rd Duke of Frías
2 CONT
2 CONT  Juan Sancho de Tovar, 1st Marquis of Berlanga
2 CONT
2 CONT  Mencía de Velasco
2 CONT
2 CONT  María de Velasco, nun
2 CONT
2 CONT  Isabel de Velasco
2 CONT
2 CONT  Juana de Velasco, nun
2 CONT
2 CONT He took part in the Castilian War of the Communities, and led the royalist army to victory at the Battle of Villalar.
2 CONT
