1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cavazos Garza, Israel.  ''Catálogo y Síntesis de los Protocolos del Archivo Municipal de Monterrey 1599-1700'', Instituto Tecnologico y de Estudios Superiores de Monterrey, Monterrey, Nuevo León, México, 1966, page
2 CONC  134, #431 [V, fol. 124, v., no. 67].  ...  This protolocolo is the '''will of Captain Miguel de la Garza Falcón'''.  It states that this document was witnessed by Lt. Nicolás de la Garza, bears no signature of the writer, and is 
2 CONC '''dated 8 May 1694''' at the Hacienda de San Francisco, Monterrey.  It states that the author is '''to be buried in the Iglesia Parroquial (Franciscan Convent of San Andrés Church now razed) in the burial place he has near the si
2 CONC de door'''.  His parents Blas de la Garza and Beatriz Gonzáles, his wife Gertrudis de Renteria, her parents Sargento Mayor Jacinto García de Sepúlveda and Doña Clara de Renteria, and his children Jacinto, Juana, Julián, Leonor, Cl
2 CONC ara, Micaela, Antonio Miguel, María, Beatriz, Félix, Juan, Pablo, and Manuel are identified.  Further, '''Juana's husband Antonio Rodríguez''', Micaela's husband Fernando Sánchez de Zamora, and María's husband Alférez Juan de Vill
2 CONC arreal are cited.
